<article class="env-lemma" id="0B51">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0B51">Lemma <span data-tag="0B51">10.62.7</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a Noetherian ring. Let $0 \to M' \to M \to M'' \to 0$ be a short exact sequence of finite $R$-modules. Then $\max \{ \dim (\text{Supp}(M')), \dim (\text{Supp}(M''))\}  = \dim (\text{Supp}(M))$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      If $R$ is local, this follows immediately from Lemmas <a href="/tag/00L8" data-tag="00L8">10.62.6</a> and <a href="/tag/00KC" data-tag="00KC">10.59.10</a>. A more elementary argument, which works also if $R$ is not local, is to use that $\text{Supp}(M')$, $\text{Supp}(M'')$, and $\text{Supp}(M)$ are closed (Lemma <a href="/tag/00L2" data-tag="00L2">10.40.5</a>) and that $\text{Supp}(M) = \text{Supp}(M') \cup \text{Supp}(M'')$ (Lemma <a href="/tag/00L3" data-tag="00L3">10.40.9</a>). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>